# Declaring a variable without an initializer is a COMPILE ERROR — Gorget has no
# uninitialized-variable form (every decl must be `Type name = value`). This is
# the negative counterpart to variable_initialization.gg. See language-design.md
# §2.1. NOTE: the diagnostic is currently the misleading "undefined name" (the
# no-`=` form falls through to expression parsing); improving it to "variable
# declaration requires an initializer" is a logged TODO papercut — when that
# lands, update the expected-stderr substring in the integration test.
void main():
    int i
    float f
    bool flag
    String s
    print(i)
